1eea3d6f-3b33-43b8-9aec-7bf9a406ac27","backgroundColor":"#0000","width":1920,"height":1080,"description":"<div><p><span>The Microsoft 365 Copilot standalone chat app (Work IQ, model Auto), signed in as Anne Krupke, with a left rail of pinned agents (Researcher, Analyst) and a chat history list. The user&apos;s prompt asks Copilot to &quot;Prepare my Daily Briefing,&quot; including pharma sector news relevant to a sourcing manager, key deadlines / due dates on open RFPs or supplier actions from the calendar, any RFP responses in the inbox, and priorities/next steps drawn from work context, formatted into sections: Industry trends, Key deadlines, Priority tasks. Copilot&apos;s response has begun with an &quot;Industry trends&quot; section: bulleted items on tariff and sourcing risk as top procurement concerns, CDMO capacity and manufacturing flexibility as strategic differentiators, regulatory and quality oversight as critical supplier-selection criteria, and notable manufacturing news (CDMO expansion by Lonza and investment in Europe), with inline source citations. A &quot;Message Copilot&quot; box sits at the bottom.</span></p></div>","presenterNotes":"<div><p><span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI;\">Some time has passed since we issued the RFP. I’m starting my day by checking out my daily digest that Copilot runs for me on a schedule, pulling industry news from the web, looking at trends in supplier performance from Fabric, and searching my work context for top priorities. </span></p><p><span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI;font-weight:bold;\">Action</span><span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI;\">: Scroll down to the bottom of the response.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI;\">This shows how Microsoft IQ-Work, Web, and Fabric IQ-all surface through the Copilot Chat experience for a well-rounded briefing. </span></p><p><span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI;\">Today’s the deadline for those RFP responses, and it looks like they’re all sitting in my inbox ready for 